{"id":"mahabharata-12-272","work":"mahabharata","part":12,"partName":"शान्तिपर्व","partNameEn":"Shanti Parva","unit":272,"title":"द्विसप्तत्यधिकद्विशततमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 272 · The battle of Indra and Vritra","summary":{"en":"Yudhishthira marvels at Vritra's devotion to Vishnu, and Bhishma tells the story of the battle, in which the gods and asuras filled the sky with weapons. The fever, the glory of Vishnu, entered Vritra, and Indra, praised by the sages, appeared in a form hard to see.","kn":"ವೃತ್ರನ ವಿಷ್ಣುಭಕ್ತಿಗೆ ಯುಧಿಷ್ಠಿರ ಆಶ್ಚರ್ಯಪಡುತ್ತಾನೆ; ದೇವ-ಅಸುರರು ಆಕಾಶವನ್ನು ಆಯುಧಗಳಿಂದ ತುಂಬಿದ ಯುದ್ಧದ ಕಥೆಯನ್ನು ಭೀಷ್ಮ ಹೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ. ವಿಷ್ಣುವಿನ ತೇಜಸ್ಸು ಜ್ವರವಾಗಿ ವೃತ್ರನನ್ನು ಪ್ರವೇಶಿಸಿತು, ಋಷಿಗಳಿಂದ ಸ್ತುತಿತ ಇಂದ್ರ ನೋಡಲಾಗದ ರೂಪದಲ್ಲಿ ಕಾಣಿಸಿದ.","hi":"युधिष्ठिर वृत्र की विष्णु-भक्ति पर विस्मित होते हैं, और भीष्म युद्ध की कथा कहते हैं जिसमें देव-असुरों ने आकाश अस्त्रों से भर दिया। विष्णु का तेज ज्वर बनकर वृत्र में समाया और ऋषियों से स्तुत इन्द्र दुर्दर्श रूप में प्रकट हुए।","te":"వృత్రుని విష్ణుభక్తికి యుధిష్ఠిరుడు ఆశ్చర్యపడతాడు; దేవాసురులు ఆకాశాన్ని ఆయుధాలతో నింపిన యుద్ధ కథను భీష్ముడు చెబుతాడు. విష్ణు తేజస్సు జ్వరంగా వృత్రునిలో ప్రవేశించింది, ఋషులచే స్తుతింపబడిన ఇంద్రుడు చూడశక్యం కాని రూపంలో కనిపించాడు.","ta":"வித்ரனின் விஷ்ணு பக்தியை யுதிஷ்டிரர் வியக்க, தேவரும் அசுரரும் வானை ஆயுதங்களால் நிரப்பிய போரின் கதையைப் பீஷ்மர் கூறுகிறார். விஷ்ணுவின் ஒளி காய்ச்சலாக வித்ரனுள் புக, முனிவர்கள் புகழ இந்திரன் காண அரிய வடிவில் தோன்றினான்.","ml":"വൃത്രന്റെ വിഷ്ണുഭക്തിയിൽ യുധിഷ്ഠിരൻ അദ്ഭുതപ്പെടുന്നു; ദേവന്മാരും അസുരന്മാരും ആകാശം ആയുധങ്ങളാൽ നിറച്ച യുദ്ധത്തിന്റെ കഥ ഭീഷ്മർ പറയുന്നു. വിഷ്ണുവിന്റെ മഹത്ത്വമായ ജ്വരം വൃത്രനിൽ പ്രവേശിച്ചു; മുനിമാർ സ്തുതിച്ച ഇന്ദ്രൻ കാണാൻ പ്രയാസമുള്ള രൂപത്തിൽ പ്രത്യക്ഷനായി."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 12.272; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Wed Jun 16 2021","sections":[{"title":"मोक्षधर्मपर्व","titleEn":"Mokshadharma Parva (Duties for liberation)","verses":[{"text":"युधिष्ठिर उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Yudhishthira said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"अहो धर्मिष्ठता तात वृत्रस्यामिततेजसः ।\nयस्य विज्ञानमतुलं विष्णोर्भक्तिश्च तादृशी ॥","meaning":{"en":"Ah, how devoted to dharma was Vritra of boundless splendor, whose knowledge was unmatched and whose devotion to Vishnu was such."}},{"n":2,"text":"दुर्विज्ञेयमिदं तात विष्णोरमिततेजसः ।\nकथं वा राजशार्दूल पदं तज्ज्ञातवानसौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"This is hard to know, dear one, about Vishnu of boundless splendor. How, tiger among kings, did he come to know that abode?"}},{"n":3,"text":"भवता कथितं ह्येतच्छ्रद्दधे चाहमच्युत ।\nभूयस्तु मे समुत्पन्ना बुद्धिरव्यक्तदर्शनात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"You have told this, Achyuta, and I believe it; but a further question has arisen in me because the unmanifest cannot be seen."}},{"n":4,"text":"कथं विनिहतो वृत्रः शक्रेण भरतर्षभ ।\nधर्मिष्ठो विष्णुभक्तश्च तत्त्वज्ञश्च पदान्वये ॥","meaning":{"en":"How was Vritra killed by Shakra, best of Bharatas, he who was righteous, a devotee of Vishnu and knower of truth in the line of that abode?"}},{"n":5,"text":"एतन्मे संशयं ब्रूहि पृच्छतो भरतर्षभ ।\nवृत्रस्तु राजशार्दूल यथा शक्रेण निर्जितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Tell me this doubt as I ask, best of Bharatas: how Vritra was defeated by Shakra."}},{"n":6,"text":"यथा चैवाभवद्युद्धं तच्चाचक्ष्व पितामह ।\nविस्तरेण महाबाहो परं कौतूहलं हि मे ॥","meaning":{"en":"And tell me, grandfather, how the battle went, in detail, mighty-armed one; my curiosity is great."}},{"text":"भीष्म उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Bhishma said:"}},{"n":7,"text":"रथेनेन्द्रः प्रयातो वै सार्धं सुरगणैः पुरा ।\nददर्शाथाग्रतो वृत्रं विष्ठितं पर्वतोपमम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Once Indra set out on a chariot together with hosts of gods, and saw Vritra standing ahead like a mountain."}},{"n":8,"text":"योजनानां शतान्यूर्ध्वं पञ्चोच्छ्रितमरिंदम ।\nशतानि विस्तरेणाथ त्रीण्येवाभ्यधिकानि तु ॥","meaning":{"en":"He stood five hundred yojanas high, scorcher of foes, and three hundred yojanas more in breadth."}},{"n":9,"text":"तत्प्रेक्ष्य तादृशं रूपं त्रैलोक्येनापि दुर्जयम् ।\nवृत्रस्य देवाः संत्रस्ता न शान्तिमुपलेभिरे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing that form of Vritra, hard to conquer even for the three worlds, the gods were terrified and found no calm."}},{"n":10,"text":"शक्रस्य तु तदा राजन्नूरुस्तम्भो व्यजायत ।\nभयाद्वृत्रस्य सहसा दृष्ट्वा तद्रूपमुत्तमम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, O king, Shakra's thighs went stiff from sudden fear of Vritra, seeing that supreme form."}},{"n":11,"text":"ततो नादः समभवद्वादित्राणां च निस्वनः ।\nदेवासुराणां सर्वेषां तस्मिन्युद्ध उपस्थिते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then a roar arose, and the sound of instruments, from all the gods and asuras as the battle began."}},{"n":12,"text":"अथ वृत्रस्य कौरव्य दृष्ट्वा शक्रमुपस्थितम् ।\nन संभ्रमो न भीः काचिदास्था वा समजायत ॥","meaning":{"en":"But Vritra, Kaurava, seeing Shakra arrive, felt no alarm or fear, nor any hesitation."}},{"n":13,"text":"ततः समभवद्युद्धं त्रैलोक्यस्य भयंकरम् ।\nशक्रस्य च सुरेन्द्रस्य वृत्रस्य च महात्मनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then there began a battle terrible to the three worlds, between Shakra, lord of the gods, and the great-souled Vritra."}},{"n":14,"text":"असिभिः पट्टिशैः शूलैः शक्तितोमरमुद्गरैः ।\nशिलाभिर्विविधाभिश्च कार्मुकैश्च महास्वनैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"With swords, battle-axes, spears, darts, lances and clubs, with many kinds of rocks and loud-twanging bows,"}},{"n":15,"text":"अस्त्रैश्च विविधैर्दिव्यैः पावकोल्काभिरेव च ।\nदेवासुरैस्ततः सैन्यैः सर्वमासीत्समाकुलम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"with various divine missiles and meteors of fire, all was filled with the armies of gods and asuras."}},{"n":16,"text":"पितामहपुरोगाश्च सर्वे देवगणास्तथा ।\nऋषयश्च महाभागास्तद्युद्धं द्रष्टुमागमन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Led by Brahma, all the hosts of gods and the great sages came to watch that battle."}},{"n":17,"text":"विमानाग्र्यैर्महाराज सिद्धाश्च भरतर्षभ ।\nगन्धर्वाश्च विमानाग्र्यैरप्सरोभिः समागमन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The perfected came in the finest aerial cars, great king, and gandharvas with apsarases in the finest cars, best of Bharatas."}},{"n":18,"text":"ततोऽन्तरिक्षमावृत्य वृत्रो धर्मभृतां वरः ।\nअश्मवर्षेण देवेन्द्रं पर्वतात्समवाकिरत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Vritra, best of upholders of dharma, filling the sky, showered Indra with a rain of stones taken from a mountain."}},{"n":19,"text":"ततो देवगणाः क्रुद्धाः सर्वतः शस्त्रवृष्टिभिः ।\nअश्मवर्षमपोहन्त वृत्रप्रेरितमाहवे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the angry hosts of gods repelled the stone rain sent by Vritra, with showers of weapons from all sides."}},{"n":20,"text":"वृत्रश्च कुरुशार्दूल महामायो महाबलः ।\nमोहयामास देवेन्द्रं मायायुद्धेन सर्वतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"And Vritra, tiger of the Kurus, of great illusion and great strength, bewildered the lord of the gods all around by illusory fighting."}},{"n":21,"text":"तस्य वृत्रार्दितस्याथ मोह आसीच्छतक्रतोः ।\nरथंतरेण तं तत्र वसिष्ठः समबोधयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Indra, afflicted by Vritra, fell into bewilderment; and Vasishtha woke him there with the Rathantara hymn."}},{"text":"वसिष्ठ उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vasishtha said:"}},{"n":22,"text":"देवश्रेष्ठोऽसि देवेन्द्र सुरारिविनिबर्हण ।\nत्रैलोक्यबलसंयुक्तः कस्माच्छक्र विषीदसि ॥","meaning":{"en":"You are the best of gods, Indra, destroyer of the gods' foes. You have the strength of the three worlds; why, Shakra, do you despair?"}},{"n":23,"text":"एष ब्रह्मा च विष्णुश्च शिवश्चैव जगत्प्रभुः ।\nसोमश्च भगवान्देवः सर्वे च परमर्षयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Here are Brahma, Vishnu, Shiva, lord of the world, and the blessed god Soma, and all the great sages."}},{"n":24,"text":"मा कार्षीः कश्मलं शक्र कश्चिदेवेतरो यथा ।\nआर्यां युद्धे मतिं कृत्वा जहि शत्रुं सुरेश्वर ॥","meaning":{"en":"Do not fall into dullness, Shakra, like some ordinary being. Fixing a noble mind on the fight, kill the enemy, lord of the gods."}},{"n":25,"text":"एष लोकगुरुस्त्र्यक्षः सर्वलोकनमस्कृतः ।\nनिरीक्षते त्वां भगवांस्त्यज मोहं सुरेश्वर ॥","meaning":{"en":"This three-eyed teacher of the world, honored by all worlds, is watching you; give up bewilderment, lord of the gods."}},{"n":26,"text":"एते ब्रह्मर्षयश्चैव बृहस्पतिपुरोगमाः ।\nस्तवेन शक्र दिव्येन स्तुवन्ति त्वां जयाय वै ॥","meaning":{"en":"These Brahmin sages, led by Brihaspati, praise you with divine hymn, Shakra, for victory."}},{"text":"भीष्म उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Bhishma said:"}},{"n":27,"text":"एवं संबोध्यमानस्य वसिष्ठेन महात्मना ।\nअतीव वासवस्यासीद्बलमुत्तमतेजसः ॥","meaning":{"en":"As he was thus awakened by the great-souled Vasishtha, the strength of Vasava, of supreme radiance, grew greatly."}},{"n":28,"text":"ततो बुद्धिमुपागम्य भगवान्पाकशासनः ।\nयोगेन महता युक्तस्तां मायां व्यपकर्षत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, regaining understanding, the blessed Paka-shasana, joined with great yoga, drew away that illusion."}},{"n":29,"text":"ततोऽङ्गिरःसुतः श्रीमांस्ते चैव परमर्षयः ।\nदृष्ट्वा वृत्रस्य विक्रान्तमुपगम्य महेश्वरम् ।\nऊचुर्वृत्रविनाशार्थं लोकानां हितकाम्यया ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the glorious son of Angiras and those great sages, seeing Vritra's prowess, approached Maheshvara and spoke for the destruction of Vritra, wishing the worlds' welfare."}},{"n":30,"text":"ततो भगवतस्तेजो ज्वरो भूत्वा जगत्पतेः ।\nसमाविशन्महारौद्रं वृत्रं दैत्यवरं तदा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the radiance of the blessed lord of the world became a fever and entered the terrible Vritra, best of Daityas."}},{"n":31,"text":"विष्णुश्च भगवान्देवः सर्वलोकाभिपूजितः ।\nऐन्द्रं समाविशद्वज्रं लोकसंरक्षणे रतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"And the blessed god Vishnu, honored by all worlds and devoted to protecting the worlds, entered Indra's thunderbolt."}},{"n":32,"text":"ततो बृहस्पतिर्धीमानुपागम्य शतक्रतुम् ।\nवसिष्ठश्च महातेजाः सर्वे च परमर्षयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the wise Brihaspati approached Shatakratu, and the very radiant Vasishtha and all the great sages as well."}},{"n":33,"text":"ते समासाद्य वरदं वासवं लोकपूजितम् ।\nऊचुरेकाग्रमनसो जहि वृत्रमिति प्रभो ॥","meaning":{"en":"Coming to Vasava, giver of boons and honored by the worlds, they said with one-pointed minds, \"Kill Vritra, lord.\""}},{"text":"महेश्वर उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Maheshvara said:"}},{"n":34,"text":"एष वृत्रो महाञ्शक्र बलेन महता वृतः ।\nविश्वात्मा सर्वगश्चैव बहुमायश्च विश्रुतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"This Vritra, Shakra, is great, surrounded by great strength, soul of the universe, all-pervading and renowned for many illusions."}},{"n":35,"text":"तदेनमसुरश्रेष्ठं त्रैलोक्येनापि दुर्जयम् ।\nजहि त्वं योगमास्थाय मावमंस्थाः सुरेश्वर ॥","meaning":{"en":"That best of asuras, hard to conquer even by the three worlds, kill, taking hold of yoga; do not despise him, lord of the gods."}},{"n":36,"text":"अनेन हि तपस्तप्तं बलार्थममराधिप ।\nषष्टिं वर्षसहस्राणि ब्रह्मा चास्मै वरं ददौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"He practiced austerity for strength, lord of the immortals, for sixty thousand years, and Brahma gave him a boon."}},{"n":37,"text":"महत्त्वं योगिनां चैव महामायत्वमेव च ।\nमहाबलत्वं च तथा तेजश्चाग्र्यं सुरेश्वर ॥","meaning":{"en":"Greatness of yogins, great illusion, great strength, and foremost radiance, lord of gods:"}},{"n":38,"text":"एतद्वै मामकं तेजः समाविशति वासव ।\nवृत्रमेनं त्वमप्येवं जहि वज्रेण दानवम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"this radiance of mine, Vasava, enters Vritra; and you also, kill this Danava with the thunderbolt."}},{"text":"शक्र उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Shakra said:"}},{"n":39,"text":"भगवंस्त्वत्प्रसादेन दितिजं सुदुरासदम् ।\nवज्रेण निहनिष्यामि पश्यतस्ते सुरर्षभ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Blessed one, by your grace I will kill the son of Diti, so hard to approach, with the thunderbolt, as you look on, best of gods."}},{"text":"भीष्म उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Bhishma said:"}},{"n":40,"text":"आविश्यमाने दैत्ये तु ज्वरेणाथ महासुरे ।\nदेवतानामृषीणां च हर्षान्नादो महानभूत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"When the great asura Daitya was entered by the fever, a great shout arose from joy among gods and sages."}},{"n":41,"text":"ततो दुन्दुभयश्चैव शङ्खाश्च सुमहास्वनाः ।\nमुरजा डिण्डिमाश्चैव प्रावाद्यन्त सहस्रशः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then drums and conches of great sound, tabors and kettledrums were sounded by the thousand."}},{"n":42,"text":"असुराणां तु सर्वेषां स्मृतिलोपोऽभवन्महान् ।\nप्रज्ञानाशश्च बलवान्क्षणेन समपद्यत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Among all the asuras there came a great loss of memory, and a mighty loss of discernment came in a moment."}},{"n":43,"text":"तमाविष्टमथो ज्ञात्वा ऋषयो देवतास्तथा ।\nस्तुवन्तः शक्रमीशानं तथा प्राचोदयन्नपि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Knowing him possessed, sages and gods praised Shakra, the lord, and urged him on."}},{"n":44,"text":"रथस्थस्य हि शक्रस्य युद्धकाले महात्मनः ।\nऋषिभिः स्तूयमानस्य रूपमासीत्सुदुर्दृशम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"As the great-souled Shakra stood in his chariot at the time of battle, praised by sages, his form was very hard to look at."}}]}]}